that right?<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">John</span>: Yeah, but Machu Picchu is a very beautiful place.<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Sally</span>: I would love to visit. Maybe after my trip to China.<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">John</span>: China? When?<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Sally</span>: Tomorrow! <br />\n<span class =\"strong\">John</span>: Wow! Have a ball!", "image": "engenn4le15ob11re2img05.jpg", "time": "45000", "id": 4}]}}]}, {"title": "", "id": 2, "template_override": 1, "type": "audio", "_data": [], "contents": [{"type": "picture", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn4le15ob11re6aud01", "coverimg": "engenn4le15ob11re6img01.jpg", "images": []}}]}, {"title": "", "id": 4, "template_override": 1, "type": "static", "_data": [], "contents": [{"type": "p", "value": "<span class =\"strong\">Sally</span>: Hey, John! <br />\n<span class =\"strong\">John</span>: Hi, Sally. How was your trip to the Grand Canyon?<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Sally</span>: That depends on who you ask. For me, it was mind-blowing! We went on an amazing 3-day hike. But \u2026<br /><br>\n<span class =\"strong\">John</span>: What happened?<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Sally</span>: Vanessa sprained her ankle and the rangers airlifted us off the cliff.<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">John</span>: Wow! Sounds crazy! <br /><br>\n\n\n<span class =\"strong\">Sally</span>: How was your trip to Machu Picchu? How far is it from Lima?<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">John</span>: Machu Picchu sits on a mountain, about 300 miles from Lima. We took a bus along twisty roads through villages.<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Sally</span>: How interesting! <br />\n<span class =\"strong\">John</span>: Yeah, the altitude is 7800 feet, so some of the tourists got altitude sickness.<br /><br>\n<span class =\"strong\">Sally</span>: Altitude sickness?! Is that right?<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">John</span>: Yeah, but Machu Picchu is a very beautiful place.<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Sally</span>: I would love to visit. Maybe after my trip to China.<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">John</span>: China? When?<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Sally</span>: Tomorrow! <br />\n<span class =\"strong\">John</span>: Wow! Have a ball!"}]}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}]}]}], "type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "John in Peru"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Hiking the Colca Canyon"}, {"type": "position", "content": 11}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 15}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Relate information about health and healthy habits in communicative situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "twisty"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "having a lot of turns in the road"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The roads are very twisty."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le15ob11aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are the words to review."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "village "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a community smaller than a town"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There are many villages along the road to Machu Picchu."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le15ob11aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "That depends on \u2026 "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the situation relies on another situation"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: That depends on how fast you climb!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le15ob11aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "altitude"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "height above the sea"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The altitude of Machu Picchu is 7870 feet."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le15ob11aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "mind-blowing"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "amazing"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Machu Picchu was mind-blowing."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le15ob11aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "Have a ball!"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "Have fun!"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I hope you have a ball in Lima."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le15ob11aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to sit"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to be located"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The city sits on the cliffs over the sea."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le15ob11aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "cliff"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a steep rock near the sea"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We have to take a bus up the cliffs."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le15ob11aud08"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "about"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "approximately"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It's about 25 miles to Lima from here."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le15ob11aud09"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn4le15ob11re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Saying How Far a Place Is"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you want to know how far a place is, you can use the question: <span class=\"italic\">How far is \u2026?</span><br />  You can reply with a specific distance if you know the answer, like <span class=\"italic\">It's 50 yards away.</span><br /> In the USA, you use the Imperial system, not the metric system.<br />   If a place is nearby, you use  <span class = \"italic\">yards</span> to say how far it is.<br />     If a place is far, you use  <span class = \"italic\">miles</span> to say how far it is."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"strong\\\"> Imperial System </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"strong\\\"> Metric System </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"1 mile \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"1.6 kilometers \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"1 yard \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"90 centimeters \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"1 foot \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"30 centimeters \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"1 inch\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"2.5 centimeters\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Showing Interest"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use these phrases and techniques to show interest and surprise in conversation:<ul>  \t<li>Use rising intonation (your voice goes up) to show interest. </li> \t<li>Use falling intonation (your voice goes down) to show surprise. </li> \t<li>Use these techniques to keep the conversation going.</li>  </ul>   \t\t\t"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"strong\\\"> Showing Interest </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"strong\\\"> Showing Surprise </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Oh?<br /> Oh yeah?<br /> Really?<br /> Oh really?<br /> Is that right?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Wow!<br /> Amazing!<br /> Get out of here!<br /> Unbelievable!<br /> No!\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Altitude sickness? Is that right? "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Vanessa sprained her ankle? No!"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Imagine you went on a trip to China or Peru."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Tell your partner about the trip."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Create two events that happened. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Ask about your partner's trip."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I talk about traveling in English."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk about details of events in the past."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I show interest and ask questions."}]}]}